 "_source": "World Bank WDI API https://api.worldbank.org/v2/country/HKG/indicator/<CODE>?format=json&per_page=100 (fetched 2026-11 via WebFetch; values rounded to 3 dp). NOTE: SE.PRM.PRIV.ZS has a definitional break between 1985 (~93%) and 1986 (~10%); pre-1986 values appear to count government-aided schools as private. Hong Kong has large net migration (mainland One-Way Permit inflows ~150/day since 1990s, plus 1997 handover/2019-2022 outflows), so cohort-survival from births/population is distorted; use C&SD age-structure data. SH.DYN.MORT and SI.POV.GINI: HKG returned all nulls (no data). SE.PRM.NENR/SE.SEC.NENR have gaps (1986-94, 1997-2000 etc.). SE.PRM.ENRR/SE.SEC.ENRR/TER: no values returned before 2001 (WDI HKG). SE.TER.ENRR 2024=120.09 looks anomalous (likely includes non-local/cross-boundary students; treat with caution). SP.DYN.CBRT.IN 2001-2012 inflated by births to mainland mothers. SE.PRM.AGES/DURS/SEC.DURS: only 1970+ returned; SEC.DURS 7 until 2011 (Forms 1-7) then 6 from 2012 (NSS). SL.EMP.WORK.ZS = wage and salaried workers % of employed, from 1991.",
